{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "20576aa5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Instructions for training in Runpod\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "bbe80cb4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "1) Launch pod, select official Runpod PyTorch template (NOT blank linux img)\n",
    "as soon as pod boots, open terminal & run:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "e9dd5c12",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "nvidia-smi"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2b473aaf",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "If not all 8 GPUs listed & working, terminate pod & deploy new"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6e49dfa5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "2) Unzip to Container Disk (temp storage):"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "272fe96d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "pip install gdown sahi ultralytics\n",
    "\n",
    "mkdir /dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "# "Google Drive link" below is the zip file of training data that I uploaded to Google Drive. I personally did this\n",
    "# so that I could easily access it from Runpod; can delete from Drive after each use since it's pretty heavy.\n",
    "\n",
    "# file ID (the stuff after 'gdown') found by:\n",
    "### Go to the Google Drive link, right-click the file share w/anyone w/link, select \"Get link\", \n",
    "### and copy the file ID from the URL (between /d/ and /view).\n",
    "\n",
    "gdown 1ag8vWlBb-jSjlbe_Twi-GgfSef7o44k4 -O /dataset/human_tree_tent_with_ours.zip\n",
    "\n",
    "# Unzip file\n",
    "unzip -q /dataset/human_tree_tent_with_ours.zip -d /dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "# Delete the zip files to free up container disk space\n",
    "rm /dataset/human_tree_tent_with_ours.zip"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b6644c3f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "3) Update data.yaml in Jupyter editor, change path line:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "46a7ceae",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# OLD (Kaggle)\n",
    "# path: /kaggle/input/dataset...\n",
    "\n",
    "# NEW (RunPod)\n",
    "path: /dataset  # Point to where you unzipped it\n",
    "train: images/train\n",
    "val: images/val"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c23307ec",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "4) Open launcher (probably blue '+' button); create text file (\"Other\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1f3c5d37",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "5) Paste post-train.py script from here into there; rename post-train.py (make sure file created in /dataset dir)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "990f3f15",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "6) For persistence (can close browser), run:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "7af70819",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "tmux"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8aee13c1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "When reopening browser, to view live progress again, run:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "f6c16987",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "tmux attach"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2c97ae85",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Code changes: dist. batch across 8 GPUs + extra augments \n",
    "(DON'T USE THIS JUPYTER NOTEBOOK CODE, USE TERMINAL COMMAND FOR PERSISTENCE)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cc58c757",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import ultralytics\n",
    "from ultralytics import YOLO\n",
    "import os\n",
    "\n",
    "# --- 1. SETUP ---\n",
    "# Ensure we are using the volume for SAVING weights (so you don't lose them)\n",
    "# Assuming you mounted your 5GB volume at /workspace/my_volume\n",
    "project_path = \"/workspace/my_volume/runs\" # CHECK THIS IS CORRECT\n",
    "\n",
    "# --- 2. LOAD MODEL ---\n",
    "# Load the pretrained model\n",
    "# model = YOLO(\"yolo11m.pt\") \n",
    "model=workspace/my_volume/best.pt\n",
    "\n",
    "# --- 3. TRAIN WITH 8 GPUs ---\n",
    "# CHANGE 'batch' AND 'device' ACCORDING TO NUMBER OF ACTUAL AVAILABLE GPUS\n",
    "# changes:\n",
    "# - device=[0,1,2...]: Enables Distributed Data Parallel (DDP) automatically\n",
    "# - batch=64: Splits to 8 images per GPU (Effective batch size of 8 per card)\n",
    "# - project: Saves results to your safe Volume disk\n",
    "# - imgsz=1024: High res for aerial accuracy\n",
    "\n",
    "results = model.train(\n",
    "    data=\"/workspace/dataset/data.yaml\",\n",
    "    epochs=125,\n",
    "    imgsz=1024,\n",
    "    batch=32,       # Total batch size (8 GPUs * 8 imgs/gpu = 64, then divide by 2 for medium model)\n",
    "    device=[0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7], # Use ALL 8 (or however many) GPUs\n",
    "    project=\"/workspace/my_volume/runs\",     # Save to persistent volume\n",
    "    name=\"run_5090_aerial\", # Name of the sub-folder\n",
    "    exist_ok=True,  # Overwrite if exists (optional)\n",
    "    warmup_epochs=0, # Disable warmup for faster start\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Accuracy Boosters\n",
    "    lr0=0.001,      # Lower learning rate for more stable training\n",
    "    conf=0.01,      # Lower confidence=more recall during training validation\n",
    "    iou=0.9,        # NMS threshold for validation (higher=keep more boxes, boosting recall)\n",
    "    max_det=300,    # Max detections per image\n",
    "    patience=25,    # Stop if no improvement for 25 epochs\n",
    "    save=True,      # Save checkpoints\n",
    "    cls=0.05        # Will classify even if not sure of exact class (boosts recall)\n",
    "\n",
    "    augment=True,   # Enable below augmentations\n",
    "    mosaic=1.0     # Enable mosaic augmentation (mixes 4 images, great for small objects)\n",
    "    rect=False,     # Disable rectangular training, keep square mosaic (more generalization)\n",
    "    degrees=8.0,   # Random rotation between -15 and +15 degrees\n",
    "    fliplr=0.1,     # Random horizontal flip with 50% chance\n",
    "    flipud=0.1     # Random vertical flip with 50% chance\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7c2a900b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "7) Run in Terminal (automatically terminates pod after training, running TTA [test time aug], and SAHI):"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "35156073",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "yolo detect train data=/dataset/data.yaml model=/workspace/my_volume/best.pt epochs=125 imgsz=1024 batch=32 device=0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7 project=/workspace/my_volume/runs name=run_5090_aerial exist_ok=True warmup_epochs=0 lr0=0.001 conf=0.01 iou=0.9 max_det=300 patience=25 save=True cls=0.05 augment=True mosaic=1.0 rect=False degrees=8.0 fliplr=0.1 flipud=0.1 && python /workspace/post-train.py && runpodctl remove pod $RUNPOD_POD_ID"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "385fdf71",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "8) After auto-termination, go to RunPod Dashboard & click Deploy; switch to cheapest GPU available (in deployment settings select the created Network Volume dropdown)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2ce8c4be",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "9) Deploy & connect to Jupyter Lab; open terminal in single GPU pod & run:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "9510b8c9",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "cd /workspace/my_volume\n",
    "\n",
    "zip -r final_results.zip runs/run_8x5090_aerial/weights/best.pt sa"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e8d5461f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "10) Navigate to /workspace/my_volume/ & download final_results.zip"
   ]
  }
 ],
